## Frontmatter & Hero

> [!TIP]
> This page's hero — the kicker, subtitle, and pills above — is produced entirely by the `kicker` / `subtitle` / `pills` frontmatter keys. `accent: "#8b5cf6"` overrides the default blue, `bg_lum: "0.0 : 0.93"` re-tunes dark and light backgrounds, and `custom_css: "./custom.css"` inlines extra styling (note the <kbd> keys across the page).

The exact frontmatter used by this document:

```yaml
---
title: "Markdown++ Capability Showcase"
accent: "#8b5cf6"
theme: "dark"
bg_lum: "0.0 : 0.93"        # or array [0.0, 0.93] or map { dark: ..., light: ... }
assets_dir: "./assets"
custom_css: "./custom.css"  # or custom_js: "./extra.js"
logo: "./assets/mdpp-logo.svg"
kicker: "Full-spectrum demonstration"
subtitle: "Every Markdown++ feature, edge case, and runtime behaviour on one page."
pills: ["dogfooding", "reference", "specimen"]
---
```

- `bg_lum` also accepts the aliases `bg-lum` and `bglum`.
- `logo` drives the navbar brand and the dynamic favicon (recolored to `--accent`).
- `custom_css` / `custom_js` are inlined into the compiled document.

